For every fixed $j\ge3$, there exists $c_j>0$ such that every symmetric $j$-tensor $H$ on $D$ satisfying $\sigma_i^{\otimes j}P_i^{\otimes j}H=P_i^{\otimes j}H$ for all $i$ obeys $$\label{eq:ent-tensor}
 \|H\|^2-\frac12\sum_{i=1}^d\|P_i^{\otimes j}H\|^2
 \ge c_j\|H\|^2 .$$

There is a deterministic $\xi>0$, depending only on $d,E$, with the following property. For every fixed $k\ge1$ and $D>0$, there are constants $C_{k,D}<\infty$ and $y_{k,D}<\infty$ such that, for every fixed $s\in\mathbb R$ and every fixed $y\ge y_{k,D}$, $$\label{eq:lim-endpoint-control}
 \limsup_{n\to\infty}
 \mathbb P\left(
 |m_n(s+\mathrm i y)-m_*|
 +\|M_{n,k}(s+\mathrm i y)-K_k(m_*)\|>y^{-\xi}
 \right)
 \le C_{k,D}y^{-D}.$$ The limit is through admissible graph sizes. The constants and the height threshold are independent of $s$; the argument $s+\mathrm i y$ is fixed before taking the limit.

