For every fixed $z\in\mathbb C_+$, $$\label{eq:sw-inner-resolvent}
 \|U_I^{-1}G_I(z)U_I^{-1}\|=O_{\mathbb P}(h),$$ and $$\label{eq:sw-second-cut}
 \mathop{\mathrm{Tr}}(D+A'-z)^{-1}
 =\mathop{\mathrm{Tr}}(D_I+A'_{II}-z)^{-1}+o_{\mathbb P}(1).$$ The same estimates hold jointly for a fixed finite list of $z$’s.

Conditional on almost every $\nu$, bounded smooth tests with bounded derivatives of finitely many trace values have expectation difference $o(1)$ between $$D_I+A'_{II}
 \quad\hbox{and}\quad
 H_r=D_I+s_1I_{q_*}+\sqrt{s_2}\,\mathcal W.$$

Suppose a sequence of deterministic diagonal matrices $V$ of dimension $m$ satisfies <a href="#eq:dbm-regularity" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:dbm-regularity">[eq:dbm-regularity]</a> and <a href="#eq:dbm-parameter-domain" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:dbm-parameter-domain">[eq:dbm-parameter-domain]</a>, with fixed constants. Fix $\sigma>0$, and suppose $$\label{eq:dbm-time-window}
 g m^\sigma\le t\le m^{-\sigma}G^2.$$ Assume also that $\rho_{\mathrm{fc},t}(0)=1/\pi$. For every fixed positive integer $a$ and $O\in C_c^\infty(\mathbb R^a)$, the difference $$\begin{aligned}
 \label{eq:dbm-marginal-test}
 &\int_{\mathbb R^a}O(\boldsymbol\alpha)
   p_{V+\sqrt t\,W_m}^{(a)}
      \left(\frac{\pi\alpha_1}{m},\ldots,
            \frac{\pi\alpha_a}{m}\right)
       \,\mathrm d\boldsymbol\alpha \notag\\
 &\hspace{12mm}-
 \int_{\mathbb R^a}O(\boldsymbol\alpha)
   p_{W_m}^{(a)}
      \left(\frac{\pi\alpha_1}{m},\ldots,
            \frac{\pi\alpha_a}{m}\right)
       \,\mathrm d\boldsymbol\alpha
 \longrightarrow0.
\end{aligned}$$ Consequently, the expected sums of $O$ over ordered tuples of distinct points of the two eigenvalue processes, both rescaled by $m/\pi$, differ by $o(1)$.
